 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "To whom",
   "texto": [
    "With verbs such as **ждать** (wait), **знать** (know), **приглашать** (invite) and **встречать** (receive or find), the person goes in accusative. To ask «Who?» you say **Кого?**: **Кого ты ждёшь?** (who are you waiting for?).",
    "Examples: **Я жду брата** (I wait for my brother), **Я знаю Анну** (I know Anna), **Я приглашаю сестру** (I invite my sister) and **Я встречаю друга** (I meet a friend)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Personal terms",
   "texto": [
    "The pronouns also change: **тебя** (you), **его** (him), **её** (her), **их** (them). It's called **Я люблю тебя** (I love you).",
    "**Любить** and **ждать** carry the same scheme: what you feel or expect goes in an accusative way."
   ]
  },
